----------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 9: METHODOLOGY NOTE
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  Attestation: LocalAuthority('pilot') issues one identity per
  source (ccao_parcel_sales, cc_assessor, tax_agency,
  sslbda_crm). The operator (Registry Signal) signs on each
  source's behalf, attesting 'retrieved from this source,
  unaltered' (public records) / 'extracted from operator's local
  pilot export, unaltered' (CRM). No county office or SSLBDA
  signed anything.

  Masses: pre-registered per source TYPE in
  pilot/mass_assignments.md, frozen at the Plan Gate BEFORE any
  snapshot was fetched. Snapshots determined only WHICH frame
  element received mass, never how much.

  Retrieval: dates, dataset ids, exact queries, and snapshot
  sha256 hashes are in pilot/MANIFEST.md. The tax source found
  no machine-readable tax record in the queried datasets; this
  statement must not be read as implying the parcel is
  tax-clear (ruling R3: the queried Treasurer dataset is a dead
  endpoint, content frozen circa 2009-2014).

  Narrative (not an observation, per I6 and ruling R4): SSLBDA
  appears in NO row of any queried public dataset for this
  parcel -- no deed, no roll year, 1999-2026. The dossier's
  not_conveyed evidence is the single field-traceable 2017 deed
  row with its printed inference (Section 1), never
  dataset-wide absence.

